Let the power of the AC be $P = 900$ watts $= 0.9$ kW.
The AC is used for $t = 8$ hours a day.
The energy consumed per day is $E = P t = 0.9 \times 8 = 7.2$ kWh.

If the time is reduced by 5 hours, the new time is $t' = 8 - 5 = 3$ hours.
The energy consumed per day with the reduced time is $E' = P t' = 0.9 \times 3 = 2.7$ kWh.

The energy saved per day is $E_s = E - E' = 7.2 - 2.7 = 4.5$ kWh.
The total energy saved in 30 days is $E_{total} = E_s \times 30 = 4.5 \times 30 = 135$ kWh.

